\section{Custom mlr3 parameters}{

\itemize{
\item \code{model} selects the pre-trained weights that are downloaded from Hugging Face, one of
\code{"LimiX-2"} (400 million parameters), \code{"LimiX-2M"} (2 million parameters), and
\code{"LimiX-16M"} (16 million parameters).
It is ignored if \code{model_path} is set.
\item \code{model_path} is the path to a local checkpoint file.
If it is not set, the checkpoint selected by \code{model} is downloaded.
\item \code{device} is a string that is passed to \code{torch.device()}, e.g., \code{"cpu"} or \code{"cuda"}.
The value \code{"auto"} selects \code{"cuda"} if it is available and \code{"cpu"} otherwise.
\item \code{inference_config} is the path to a JSON file with the inference configuration.
If it is not set, the default configuration without retrieval that ships with \code{LimiX} is used,
depending on the task type and the architecture version of the checkpoint.
\item \code{cache_dir}, \code{test_batch_mode}, \code{test_batch_size}, \code{enable_preprocess_parallel}, \code{preprocess_num_jobs},
and \code{gpu_ids} are only used by \code{"LimiX-2"}.
\code{LimiX} prints a warning and ignores them for the other models.
\item \code{test_batch_size} accepts either an integer or the special value \code{"None"}
which corresponds to \code{None} in Python.
\item \code{gpu_ids} accepts an integer vector of CUDA device indices, using the zero-based indexing of Python.
\item \code{categorical_features_indices} and \code{inference_with_DDP} are not available,
because the first is not used by \code{LimiX} for classification and regression,
and the second requires a distributed setup.
}
}

